WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.270
Speaker 1: We have a voicemail number.

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:04.540
That number is 2192.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:12.420
David P Here is a really great question about
how to deal with people who do a certain really

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.679
annoying thing during political debates, in
conversations.

00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:15.679
Take a listen.

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:16.679
Speaker 6: Hey, David.

00:00:16.679 --> 00:00:17.679
Sir, this is Jose.

00:00:17.679 --> 00:00:18.679
I just had a quick question.

00:00:18.679 --> 00:00:19.679
Yes.

00:00:19.679 --> 00:00:26.770
I was wondering if you had any advice to what
you would tell somebody to having a discussion

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:31.140
with them about politics, where they just
immediately go to what about Islam?

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.800
They don't really bring anything to the conversation.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.660
They just say, what about this?

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.660
What about that?

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.660
What about this?

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.750
Yeah, this needs some help just with that.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.020
Speaker 1: Thank you.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.410
So this is super common.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:50.340
The way it might go is you say, listen, the
evidence is indicative that Trump committed

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.000
crimes and should be charged.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.930
And then the person you're talking to goes,
well, what about Hunter Biden?

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:03.519
Understand that sometimes when people do the
what about this other thing, it's because

00:01:03.519 --> 00:01:04.830
their brain is scrambled.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:08.259
And I'm not saying this to make fun of people,
but what I mean is there are lots of people

00:01:08.259 --> 00:01:15.380
who they don't organize their thoughts in
their head and they can't think straight.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.200
And so they're just bouncing all over the
place.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.990
And it's sort of like a cognitive issue of
getting them to actually focus in on.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:26.979
The one thing you're trying to talk about,
that's one category.

00:01:26.979 --> 00:01:34.040
You then also have people who use what about
ism as deliberate deception or to try to undermine

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.009
or distract and create red herrings.

00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:40.850
They use it sort of like as a tool, very deliberately
and in bad faith.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:45.479
And then you've got people who it's not that
their brain is totally scrambled and they're

00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:47.329
not completely bad faith.

00:01:47.329 --> 00:01:51.450
They're just kind of like a little ignorant
and they don't realize that there's all these

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:55.530
separate issues and we should deal with these
issues one at a time.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:02:01.670
So the step one is sort of try to figure out
if the person doing the whataboutism is doing

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:07.549
it for one or the other of those possibilities
that I mentioned, bad faith, brain scrambled,

00:02:07.549 --> 00:02:09.110
sort of confused.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:10.580
Try to figure that out.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:15.450
And one of the best tools that I find when
somebody brings out this other thing that

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.060
they want to talk about is to say, hey, you
know what?

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.840
That may also be a problem.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.040
I'm glad to talk about that.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.770
But let's stick with this topic first.

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:29.450
Resolve it and then we can talk about that
other thing very quickly.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:33.810
You'll know if you say something like that
when the what about ism pops up, whether you're

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:38.880
dealing with a brain scramble or someone functioning
in bad faith or someone who's just a little

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.230
bit confused, and sometimes they'll say, Oh,
you know what?

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:42.230
You're right.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:44.540
Okay, yeah, let's figure this thing out first.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:48.709
Then we can talk about that other thing, another
tool.

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:49.830
These aren't even really tools.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:53.550
These are literally just one liners to try
to refocus the conversation.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:57.930
Another thing that can sometimes be said when
the whataboutism pops up is something along

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:01.800
the lines of Can we just decide and agree
what we're talking about now?

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:02.849
I know there is all.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.530
These different things we can talk about.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.349
You're wanting to talk about something different.

00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:10.220
Let's just agree what we're now talking about.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:13.959
And oftentimes it'll get the other person
to have to actually tell you what it is we're

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:15.140
talking about.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:18.270
And if they're doing a what about ism with
something that really isn't related?

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:22.849
But what about that time when Obama drew a
red line in Syria?

00:03:22.849 --> 00:03:26.069
Doesn't really have anything to do with the
Qatari World Cup, does it?

00:03:26.069 --> 00:03:27.069
Right.

00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:32.370
The example sometimes that will also get people
refocus because you're letting them decide

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:33.670
what you're talking about.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:36.800
And sometimes it'll become evident that the
two things aren't related.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.360
If you're trying to talk about criminal charges
against Trump and they want to talk about

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:45.140
Obama's red line, and you say, can you just
tell me what are we talking about right now?

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:48.730
Just so we can finish that, it's going to
be hard for them to go.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:53.730
Well, we're talking about criminal charges
against Trump and Obama's red line in Syria.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:57.620
A lot of people, when they say that out loud,
would go, wait a second, that those two things

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.290
aren't even remotely connected.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:00.530
That doesn't make any sense.

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:01.530
Okay.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:05.190
So some ideas for dealing with the what about
lists?

